From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dvdvideocodecffmpeg: reuse active hardware decoder on identical get_format

When decoding HEVC bitstreams with in-band parameter sets (e.g. Dolby
Vision Profile 5 streams where every GOP carries VPS/PPS with varying
trailer metadata), FFmpeg invalidates parameter sets and calls get_format()
periodically (every ~5 seconds). Kodi unconditionally destroyed and
reallocated the active hardware decoder, causing heavy surface allocation
churn, DMA-BUF identity cache thrashing, and dropping all in-flight reference
frames across decoder generations.

This patch adds Reopen() to IHardwareDecoder and implements it for VAAPI.
When get_format() is requested with compatible parameters (matching
dimensions, bit depth, and profile), the existing VAAPI decoder context
and surface pool are reused directly. Only a new AVHWFramesContext referencing
the existing surface pool is attached to the AVCodecContext, eliminating
playback stutter without reallocating hardware surfaces or dropping frames.

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodec.h b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodec.h
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodec.h
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodec.h
@@ -377,6 +377,7 @@ public:
   IHardwareDecoder() = default;
   ~IHardwareDecoder() override = default;
   virtual bool Open(AVCodecContext* avctx, AVCodecContext* mainctx, const enum AVPixelFormat) = 0;
+  virtual bool Reopen(AVCodecContext* avctx, AVCodecContext* mainctx, const enum AVPixelFormat fmt) { return false; }
   virtual CDVDVideoCodec::VCReturn Decode(AVCodecContext* avctx, AVFrame* frame) = 0;
   virtual bool GetPicture(AVCodecContext* avctx, VideoPicture* picture) = 0;
   virtual CDVDVideoCodec::VCReturn Check(AVCodecContext* avctx) = 0;
diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecFFmpeg.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecFFmpeg.cpp
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecFFmpeg.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecFFmpeg.cpp
@@ -340,6 +340,18 @@ enum AVPixelFormat CDVDVideoCodecFFmpeg::GetFormat(struct AVCodecContext * avctx
   // hardware decoder de-selected, restore standard ffmpeg
   if (ctx->HasHardware())
   {
+    const AVPixelFormat* cur = fmt;
+    while (*cur != AV_PIX_FMT_NONE)
+    {
+      if (ctx->m_pHardware->Reopen(avctx, ctx->m_pCodecContext, *cur))
+      {
+        pixFmtName = av_get_pix_fmt_name(*cur);
+        ctx->m_processInfo.SetVideoPixelFormat(pixFmtName ? pixFmtName : "");
+        return *cur;
+      }
+      cur++;
+    }
+
     ctx->SetHardware(nullptr);
     avctx->get_buffer2 = avcodec_default_get_buffer2;
     avctx->slice_flags = 0;
